# Xcode

## User settings
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint

## Build products
build/
DerivedData/
dist/
*.ipa
*.pkg
*.dmg
*.xcarchive
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

## Code coverage / profiling artifacts (instrumented test/build runs)
*.profraw
*.profdata
*.gcda
*.gcno

## Swift Package Manager
.swiftpm/
.build/

## Signing material — never belongs in source control
*.p12
*.cer
*.mobileprovision

## Secrets / local env overrides
*.env
*.env.*
.env

## OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## Playwright MCP
.playwright-mcp/

## Local Claude Code tooling state — session data and worktree scratch copies, not project source
.claude/

## Research reference clones — large, disposable, easily re-cloned. The NOTES.md/README.md docs
## alongside them are the actual durable output and should still be tracked normally.
references/*/repo/
## Third-party competitor app binaries/DMGs gathered for local resource-usage comparison — not
## ours to redistribute, and not project source.
references/dmgs/
